notes.notes:
Steam Cards
Now the game will reward you with Trading Cards that can be collected to craft Steam Badges. We are also adding other community items like Backgrounds and Emoticons in this update.

General Update
Stats will no longer show for bonuses that are equal to zero for better readability;
Temporary Upgrades are slightly more likely to appear;
Temporary Upgrades can appear on the 5th wave onwards (was between the waves 10 and 25);
Whenever you reach the amount of cheese necessary to win a wave you automatically become invulnerable to prevent frustrating deaths due to unfortunate timing;
Cheese to reach the wave threshold is now added immediately upon an enemy's death, instead of when the cheese is collected by you;
Now, the 30th Wave will also grant you an upgrade;
Curse Damage will also benefit from extra damage taken by enemies;
New songs were added.

Upgrades Collection
The Upgrades Collection can now be scrolled through by clicking with the mouse.

Waves
Amount of cheese necessary on Waves 30+ decreased from 250 to 50.

Upgrades
Changes
Ammo V: Increases projectile damage by 200% of your ammo (was 50%);
Impact VI: Reduced shot spread by 30%.

New Upgrades
Star Arrow X: Your star allies can also summon arrows;
Debuff Master X: Your debuff damage is increased by 100%. Your debuff speed is increased by 100%;

Glass Heart ???: Your total amount of hearts are reduced to 1.0. Your total bonus projectile damage is multiplied by 2.0;
Unalterable Critical ???: Your critical damage is always at 300%;
Speed Transmutation ???: All your bonus movement speed is transformed into critical chance;
Silver Bullet ???: Decreases your total ammo by 99%. Increases your projectile penetration by 9876%. Increases projectile damage by 250%;
Cursed Cannons ???: Your reload time takes 2.0 times longer. Your number of shots is 3.0 times bigger.

Characters
Mr. Lucky
Swapped some skills around the skill tree;

Increases upgrade options and roll count by 1. Whenever you roll, your projectile damage and reload speed increase by 3% (REMOVED);

During the waves of number: 5, 15, 25, you gain one extra upgrade (NEW);
Increases upgrade options and roll count by 1 (NEW);
Whenever you roll, your projectile damage and reload speed increase by 3% (NEW);

Increases projectile damage by 50% (was 20%);
Increases the amount of cheese that enemies drop by 50% (was Increases movement speed by 20%);
Every 3 waves, randomly increase your projectile damage, fire rate, reload speed, ammo or critical damage by 25% (was Increases projectile damage, fire rate, reload speed, ammo and critical damage by 25%);
Increases critical damage by 50% for every rare upgrade you have (was Increases projectile damage by 10% for every upgrade you have);

Soldier
Every 3 waves, you gain 40% extra ammo (was Every 5 waves);
Increases shot number by 3. Increases ammo by 100%. Whenever you kill 3 enemies, the 2 closest enemies die (was Increases shot number by 3. Increases ammo by 40%);
Increases fire rate by 50%. Increases reload speed by 40%. Whenever you kill 3 enemies, the 2 closest enemies die (was Increases fire rate by 50%. Increases reload speed by 40%. Increases ammo by 30%).

Doctor
Your poison damage is increased by 50%. Your poison speed is increased by 50% (was Every 5 waves, you gain 10% extra poison damage);
Every 5 waves, you gain 50% poison speed (was Your poison damage and poison speed is increased by 30% and 100%, respectively);
Every 5 waves, you gain 50% poison damage (was Your poison damage and poison speed is increased by 100% and 30%, respectively);
Every 5 waves, you gain 40% extra curse speed (was 10%);
Every 5 waves, cursed enemies take 50% extra damage (was 15%).

M1C3
Swapped some skills around the skill tree;

Increases fire rate by 40% (REMOVED);
You don't get upgrades for 5 waves. After that you get 3 upgrades for 5 waves(REMOVED);

Increases knockback by 100% (was 50%);
Increases critical damage by 100% (was 50%);
Gear upgrades are more likely to appear. Gear upgrades can show up repeatedly throughout a run. Gear upgrades will grant you additional upgrades on wave 20 (was After 5 waves, you get the Gear V and 2 extra upgrades)
Replaces all your hearts with metal hearts. For every metal half heart, increases your projectile damage and your projectile penetration by 60% (was For every half heart missing);
After standing still for 3 seconds, your gain 150% increased fire rate, and 150% arrow damage (was 100% and 150%, respectively).

Mr. Shock
 Swapped some skills around the skill tree;

Every 20th hit to an enemy increases your lightning damage by 1% (was Every 15th hit);
Your lightnings area damage is 100% bigger in size (was You summon 1 extra lightnings)
Increases fire rate by 50% (was 20%);
Your lightnings also stun enemies for 0.8 seconds (was for 0.5 seconds);
Your lightning damage is increased by 50%. Increases fire rate by 50%. (was 20% and 20%, respectively]);
Every 8 waves, you summon 1 extra lightnings (was Every 10 waves).

Bug Fixes
Fixed some localization issues;
Fixed a bug where Curse spread from the Curse III Upgrade sometimes wouldn't spread.

General Update
- Reduced the delay for the enemies to start showing up after selecting an upgrade;

- Perfuration X: Now also increases projectile penetration of Star Projectiles and Arrow Projectiles;

Bug Fixes
- Fixed an issue where if you already had all the achievements you wouldn't be able to get the Cheese Moon achievement;
- Fixed some localization issues;

General Update
- Added a menu option to disable automatic pause when tabbed out;
- Added a menu option to restart a run;
- You can now see the enemy health increase and enemy speed increase in the stats menu along with your stat increases;
- You can now see the shot number increase in the stats menu;
- Now the game will teach you how to show game stats for the first time;
- Added an achievement when you unlock all the achievements.

Waves 30+
- Number of cheese necessary between waves decreased from 800 to 250;
- Enemy health and speed scaling decreased, and scale changed from linear to exponential.

Characters
Mr. Shock
- Your lightning damage is increased by 100% (was 20%);
- Every 15th hit to an enemy increases your lightning damage by 1% (was Every 25th enemy killed increases your lightning damage by 1%).

Upgrades
- Gear Upgrades can now be collected in multiple quantities (before that, whenever you got a Gear Upgrade it would no longer show up any of the other Gear Upgrades).
- Rare Upgrades are now named;
- Rare Upgrades are now easier to find;
- Combo Upgrades now have a unique card background and sound effect when showing up;

- Curse III: Whenever you take damage or dodge, you inflict curse on all enemies nearby (now also spreads curse when successfully dodging);
- Health V: Every 200th enemy killed heals you by 0.5 hearts (now only counts down enemies when not full on health);
- Critical V: Hitting a critical shot empowers your next attack with a 60% increased critical damage (no longer caps at 1000% and swapped with Critical VII);
- Critical VII: Whenever a shot kills an enemy with a critical hit, it increases your next attack's shot number by 1 (swapped with Critical V);
- Overload: Increases all damage sources by 100% (was Increases all damage sources by 40%, and now also increases curse damage).

Bug Fixes
- Fixed and issue where fully upgrading one skill tree then buying a single skill from other skill trees would incorrectly prompt you with an achievement;
- Fixed an issue where the game could crash when choosing upgrades with the arrow keys on the keyboard.

Dev Notes
One of the most asked additions is finally here, which is an Upgrade Collection to see whichever upgrades are left for The Collector achievement. Aside from that, these are mostly a bunch of changes of quality life to make the experience better, a bit of balancing where it was needed, adjustments to the Waves beyond 30 that felt too frustrating way too quickly.

I also felt like adding an achievement to have all achievement was a good idea so whenever we have Profile Features available for the game you'll be able to show it off on your profile. If you already have all the achievements and is missing this one, you just have to open the game and it should pop off.

I hope you folks enjoy it. I've been having a blast from the amount of love I've been receiving from you all playing the game so I felt the need to make this update live ASAP.
